Yo, fellow nethaddicts;

Everybody wants to know when Nethack 3.1 is coming out, including me.
I haven't the foggiest, and I'm not on the dev team, but here are
a few tidbits just to whet your appetite on what's coming.

I was *REAL* tired of trodding endlessly through maze levels in Hell,
so I got interested in designing my own special level, akin to the
castle and Vlad tower levels. I drew up something interesting and sent
it to the dev team. I got a couple of replies from the dev team people,
and here is what they said.
1) First, Hell is undergoing some major transformations. They didn't
say any more, but I think we can really look forward to something new
and exciting. I'm sure there will be *some* mazes left, but smart money
is on a much smaller fraction of them than is currently the case.
2) My level design was deemed not to suit the new philosophy of Hell
(whatever that means), but the dev team liked it and said they would
incorporate it somewhere else in the dungeon. Let me just say that this
particular level will *not* please people who hate falling into water,
and that it features a fiercely guarded former residence of the Wizard
Himself (with lots of magical goodies left behind), plus a tourist
office in the middle of nowhere. There are many surprises awaiting the
unwary traveller, but you'll just have to wait to find out what they are.

Anyway, yes, it *is* taking a long time for 3.1 to get released, but I
think the wait is well worth it. Why don't those of you out there who
have some inkling of what's to come post a few hints about what we can
expect? It might make the wait more bearable. On the other hand, it might
make it worse...

Stephane Coutu
(I only hope 3.1 is released *after* I finish writing my thesis...)




